35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"The roads closed for eleven days, yet the halls kept their evening timetables. That resilience is what I need to understand.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The bus cuts mean an hour’s trip to a counter. Yet remote use peaks after nine, when we lock up.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,I found the old digitisation project left half the images unindexed! But the evening groups still meet. Why do we ignore that?,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The grant covers sessions for a year, then the flat budget absorbs them. Meanwhile, vehicle costs overran by a third. That’s the trap.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The register shows a dozen retired tradespeople, but zero staff trained to supervise outside facilitators. We cannot add duties without that skill set.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Rin, those evening groups surviving is wonderful. It shows people will gather if we simply provide the space, without needing complex logistics.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, that resilience is key. But the bus cuts mean an hour’s trip to a counter. Yet remote use peaks after nine, when we lock up.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Jonathan, wait! If people are already gathering on their own, why do we need a fancy new program? We just need to stop ignoring what works!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, the groups survive because they are self-sustaining. Our budget isn’t. I’m watching the grant terms, not the sentiment.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, I see the funding trap. But my data shows a skills gap. We lack supervisors for outside facilitators. We cannot just add duties.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, that is a serious worry. We must ensure we have the right people to guide these new activities safely.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, that gap is real. But my data shows demand peaks when we are closed. We must address the access barrier before adding more duties.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Minako, wait! If the tradespeople are already running the clinic, why do we need new supervisors? We just need to trust them!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, trust is not a supervision protocol. If the grant lapses, who signs off on safety? I need a structure, not just goodwill.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Rin, trust is not a safety protocol. The technician who certified the tools retired. We lack the specific oversight skills to manage external facilitators safely.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I am glad we are finding common ground. The halls kept their timetables despite the snow. That steady, local rhythm is what I hope to see in our new plans.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"The access gap is stark. We lock up at nine, yet demand peaks later. We must fix who can reach us before adding more programs.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Benjamin, but the groups proved they work without us! Why keep paying for things that fail when people already do it themselves?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, self-sustaining means zero recurring cost. My data shows recurring costs are where the budget bleeds. I’m not paying for sentiment; I’m paying for sustainability.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, agreed. But the tool certification gap is critical. Without that specific oversight, we cannot safely manage external facilitators.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
