60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I am drawn to the Mobile Branch. It brings us to the outer wards, respecting the local rhythm we discussed.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The bus cuts leave an hour’s gap. A mobile unit closes that distance, unlike a portal or workshop.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Benjamin, the old scan project failed! I won’t pick D. But C sounds like the groups that already work.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, D’s failure was execution, not concept. But A’s vehicle costs overran by a third. I’m wary of recurring transport liabilities.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, A’s vehicle costs are a liability, but B’s tool certification gap is a safety risk. I cannot support B without trained supervisors.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, I understand your caution. But the halls proved that local rhythm survives even when roads close. A mobile unit brings that steady presence to those who cannot reach us.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, I agree. The mobile unit directly addresses the access gap I found. It reaches those cut off by the bus cuts, unlike the other options.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Minako, but the tradespeople are already running the clinic! Why do we need new supervisors? We just need to trust them!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, trust doesn’t sign the liability waiver. @Minako, B is a safety minefield. @Shizue, A’s recurring costs are a budgetary hemorrhage. I’m leaning C, but I need to see the facilitator structure.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Minako"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, C requires trained facilitators. My data shows zero staff trained to supervise them. We lack the specific oversight skills to manage external partners safely.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, I hear your worry. But the halls kept their timetables without us. Perhaps we can trust the community to help guide these circles, as they did before.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, the access gap is the primary barrier. A mobile unit reaches those cut off by the bus cuts, unlike the other options.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Minako, but the evening groups already work without us! Why add more staff when people are already doing it?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, C’s recurring fees hit the flat budget after year one. That’s the trap. I’m voting C, but only if we cap the scope.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, C is a recurring cost trap. @Shizue, A ignores the access gap. I am voting D, as it avoids the staffing and transport liabilities we cannot cover.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"I am voting for the Mobile Branch. It brings the library to those who cannot reach us, honoring the steady rhythm of our community.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I am voting for the Mobile Branch. It directly closes the access gap I identified, reaching those cut off by the bus cuts.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,I am voting for Language Learning Circles! The old groups proved people will gather on their own. We just need to stop ignoring what already works!,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I am voting for the Digital Archive Portal. It avoids the recurring transport and staffing liabilities that would bleed our flat budget dry in year two.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minako,,I am voting for the Digital Archive Portal. It avoids the staffing and transport liabilities we cannot cover.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
